From 170bc300b2d3ec61a71ff922e3c28b44903beea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steffen Deusch <steffen@deusch.me>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] brush: exec, trap and kill on WASI

exec applies its redirections as on unix; a command runs as a child, then
the shell exits with its status. Signals are POSIX's, numbered as Linux's,
for trap and kill; kill sends one through the host's processes.
